# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v2 hardening. github.com/ybkim95/TeamBench is PUBLIC (4 forks), so anything
# below is excluded by rule rather than by remembering.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Credentials. .env is already ignored above; these are the others that exist
# on disk and are NOT duplicated in it.
/api_keys.txt
*.pem
*.key
serviceAccount*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Human study. Contains participant identifiers, including MIT addresses, and is
# covered by IRB exempt determination 7676. Excluded WHOLESALE and with no
# exceptions: a `!` rule cannot re-include a file under an ignored directory, so
# exception lists here give a false sense of safety and would silently break the
# moment a new subdirectory appears.
#
# Whatever is publishable is COPIED, after a PII check, to
# shared/paper/human_study/ which is tracked. Deny by default, publish by
# explicit act.
/human_eval/

# Build caches and interpreters fetched at setup time. 78 GB.
.cache/
.venv/
/venv_*/
/teambench-ml/
/teambench-ds/
/teambench/
node_modules/

# Agent run artifacts. Regenerated by running the experiments.
shared/runs/
shared/ablation_runs/
shared/campaigns/
shared/hidden_runs/
experiments/*/runs/
experiments/*/ablation_runs/

# Scratch experiments from earlier projects, not part of TeamBench
/acorn_*
/baseline_benchmarks/
/tasks_quarantine/
/scheduler/
*.output
.zero.txt
.specsplit.txt

# Reviewer correspondence is not ours to publish
/paper/comments/

# Stray files from an interrupted `pip install foo>=1.2.0` (shell ate the >)
=*

# Scratch notes from earlier sessions
.lb90graders.txt
.ghlb90.txt
.counts2.txt
.*.txt

# NFS silly-rename turds and local agent config
/.claude/
.nfs*

# Manuscripts. Drafts stay local: they are not needed to reproduce anything,
# and a directory named for a venue and year would announce where this work is
# going next. The v2 manuscript is the exception and IS tracked, under a
# venue-neutral name, because it is the writeup of everything in this branch.
#
# `/paper/*` rather than `/paper/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so a `!` exception under one has no effect.
#
# The exception is `paper/manuscript/`, not `paper/v2/`: a `paper/v2/` already
# existed as one of the old v1..v7 drafts, complete with venue-named style files,
# and un-ignoring it would have published those.
/paper/*
!/paper/manuscript/
!/paper/EXPERIMENT_FACTSHEET.md

# Budget sweep run artifacts: 19,793 files of per-run agent workspaces, which
# are regenerated by rerunning the sweep. Only the workspaces are excluded. The
# result JSONs and their checkpoints ARE the experimental record and are kept:
# a sweep selection's directory is 880K of pure results now that runs are staged
# on local disk via TEAMBENCH_RUNS_DIR.
shared/ablation_results/*/ablation_runs/
shared/ablation_results/**/ablation_runs/
shared/ablation_results/**/workspace/
shared/ablation_results/**/logs/

# Superseded manuscript tree. Directory names here name venues and years.
/paper_old/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# shared/ is deny-by-default. It holds 130,000+ per-run agent artifacts
# (role_ablation 87,990 files, the gemma campaigns, budget-sweep workspaces)
# which are regenerated by rerunning an experiment. Only the consolidated
# records are kept, and they are named explicitly.
#
# Each directory must be un-ignored before a rule inside it can apply: git does
# not descend into an ignored directory, so a `!` under one has no effect.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/shared/*
!/shared/*.json
!/shared/paper/
!/shared/ablation_results/
/shared/ablation_results/*
!/shared/ablation_results/*.json
!/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/
/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/*
!/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/*/
/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/*/*
!/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/*/*.json
!/shared/ablation_results/budget_sweep/*/*.jsonl
!/shared/ea_results/
/shared/ea_results/*
!/shared/ea_results/*.json

# GH task workspaces. They are fragments of upstream repositories: only the
# files a pull request touched, which is the root cause of the corpus never
# measuring anything, and vendoring them puts AGPL-3.0, GPL-3.0 and LGPL-3.0
# code under this repository's MIT licence with no NOTICE files.
#
# curation_notes.json (repo + base_sha) and reference/patch.diff ARE tracked, so
# any GH workspace is reconstructible: harness/core_staging.py clones the real
# repository at base_sha. Nothing is lost except the vendoring.
tasks/GH*/workspace/

# Grader scratch output, written during a run
tasks/*/reports/
tasks/*/reports_tmp/

# Interface feedback correspondence and review notes. Not needed to reproduce
# anything, and some of it names where the work has been submitted.
/_local_feedback_archive/
/iterace_feedbacks/

# Editor/script backups. gen_*.py.bak also trip secret scanners on synthetic
# fixture keys: an AWS documentation placeholder and a public CI token from the
# transformers test suite. Noise a reviewer should not have to triage.
*.bak

# Internal planning documents. Not needed to reproduce anything, and several
# name where the work has been submitted.
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/*CHECKLIST.md

# Root-level working files that are not part of the benchmark. Three of them
# name a submission venue, and none is needed to reproduce anything.
/ACTION_PLAN.md
/collaborator_update.md
/croissant_for_openreview.json
/etc.py
/feedbacks.txt
/patch_gemma4.py
/renaming_plan.md
/repo_file_list.json

# A nested git repository. Committed it would become a gitlink (mode 160000)
# with no .gitmodules entry, so a fresh clone gets an empty directory and
# `git submodule update` fails.
/tasks/GH120_redis-py_3863_clone/
